> ```
> together with the polynomiality of `Q` (cancellation of the `π^{-1}`-tail).
> Bounded quantity: (a)+(b)+(c) is exactly the datum Appendix II uses, and
> the conjecture is that it suffices **uniformly in `k`**.

The cheapest test of the conjecture: instantiate (a)–(c) on **G2**
