   350	`c09d9f0b8b7e763734c42d5c7cf69ca9adfd41d25ae53a3dbbbe1896badacae1`).
   351	
   352	The exact replay input has SHA-256
   353	`fc2c504604c51e33e7c63e32bde4a952d0c6741b99fcf5e9c334c63eefb4796b`,
   354	identical to the charged decisive input. Singular 4.3.2 `std` returns
   355	
   356	```text
   357	MAIN_START ... residual_equations=6 residual_unknowns=3
   358	MAIN_DONE basis_size=
   359	1
   360	MAIN_QUADRATIC_FIELD_EMPTY
   361	G[1]=1
   362	```
   363	
   364	in 0.06 s with 12,988 KiB maximum RSS and empty stderr.
   365	
   366	### 3.4 `t=4`: `(52,36;49;3)`
   367	
   368	Here `x=q5_1`, `y=q9_1`, and
   369	
   370	```text
   371	H_4=486y^2-270y+35,
   372	c=y(130-1404y)/2187.
   373	```
   374	
   375	Sixteen exact Q-pivots reduce the 65-row/45-unknown chart to 48 rows in 29
   376	unknowns. After the slice, exact duplicate removal, and passage to
   377	`Q[y]/(H_4)`, there are 38 rows in 26 auxiliaries. Twenty-two further
   378	unit-only affine pivots leave eight generators in four variables
   379	`(b3,b4,a2_0,q3_0)`, one at each band `h=0,...,7`, all with remainder tag
   380	`(gamma_power,pi_power)=(0,1)`, and degrees `17,16,...,10`. The appearance of
   381	`q3_0` rather than `a3_0` is a valid pivot-coordinate choice, not an invariant
   382	naming claim.
   383	
   384	`PENDING_T4_EXACT_BASIS`
   385	
   386	The previously charged full-chart bases `[1]` over three good primes remain
   387	**MEASURED-MODULAR** only. The structural reductions just listed are exact in
   388	characteristic zero whether or not the final basis computation completes.
   389	
   390	## 4. The residual pattern and the exact blocker
   391	
   392	### 4.1 What the finite systems actually say
   393	
   394	The proposed statement
   395	
   396	```text
   397	six generators in (b3,b4,a2_0), bands 0,...,5, for every t
   398	```
   399	
   400	is false, not merely unproved. Both `t=1` and `t=2` are counterexamples to
   401	that presentation; at `t=2`, `a2_0` is eliminated by the required gauge.
   402	
   403	The exact `t=2,3,4` reductions instead exhibit the tentative linear pattern
   404	
   405	```text
   406	post-H/c input:       9t+2 rows in 6t+2 auxiliaries,
   407	affine pivots:        5t+2,
   408	zero/duplicate rows:  2t,
   409	terminal:             2t rows in t variables,
   410	bands:                0,...,2t-1,
   411	degrees:              4t+1,...,2t+2.
   412	```
   413	
   414	This is exact for the three displayed integers, but is **not** promoted as an
   415	all-`t` theorem. Residual coordinate names depend on the chosen valid pivot
   416	sequence, and no closed second-spine recurrence has been proved.
   417	
   418	### 4.2 Smallest proved uniform statement
   419	
   420	The following much smaller statement is proved uniformly:
   421	
   422	1. The banded chart, coefficient spaces, and three gauges are valid for all
   423	   `t>=1` and contain no parameter denominators.
   424	2. There are `3t+4` Q-constant quotient pivots, descending from band
   425	   `4t+1` through band `2t`. The gauged chart has `9t+9` variables, so this
   426	   leaves `6t+5` before the weighted slice.
   427	3. The positive grading, equations (H) and (C), the `x=1` equivalence, and
   428	   the c-unit statement in the separable algebra `A_t` hold for every
   429	   positive integer `t`.
   430	4. No fixed collection of low bands, or of low plus a fixed number of
   431	   extreme-high bands, can supply a uniform unit certificate: the charged
   432	   exact point
   433	   `Q=h^q+B, P=h^e+2pi-gamma, c=-1` satisfies all low levels through
   434	   `2t-1` and fails only at the moving bands `2t` and `3t+1`.
   435	
   436	The missing object is the **second affine spine in the t-scaling middle**.
   437	After passage to `A_t`, every proposed pivot coefficient is an element
   438	`u_(t,j)(y)`. A uniform quotient-ring elimination must give a closed formula
   439	or recurrence for these elements and prove
   440	
   441	```text
   442	Norm_(A_t/Q)(u_(t,j))=Res_y(H_t,u_(t,j)) != 0
   443	```
   444	
   445	for every required band index and every positive integer `t`. It must also
   446	prove the observed duplicate/zero recurrence and identify the growing
   447	terminal ideal. The coefficient-space boundaries move at low band `t` and at
   448	high offset `t`; this is precisely where the charts for `t` and `t+1` first
   449	differ. Thus the normalizer is no longer the blocker. The growing middle
   450	ideal is.
   451	
   452	## 5. Why a generic-`t` `[1]` is not presently available
   453	
   454	There is no fixed six-by-three residual `R_t` to enter in
   455	`Q(t)[y]/(H_t)`: the verified terminal rings and generator sets grow with
   456	`t`. One could encode them by an indexed recurrence, but that recurrence is
   457	the open second-spine problem just named. Consequently no generic Gröbner
   458	basis was computed and no finite exceptional denominator set is asserted.
   459	
   460	If a future recurrence or genuinely fixed reformulation does yield
   461	
   462	```text
   463	1=sum_i A_i(t,y,z) R_i(t,y,z)+B(t,y,z)H_t(y)
   464	```
   465	
   466	over `Q(t)`, FALLACY-v2 requires clearing a common nonzero denominator
   467	`D(t)`. The certificate specializes only when `D(t0)` and the leading
   468	coefficient of `H_t0` are nonzero. Every inverted `A_t` coefficient must
   469	contribute its norm/resultant to `D`, and every integer root of `D` must be
   470	handled exactly.
   471	
   472	The infinite split set `t=3s^2-1` is not a finite denominator-exception set.
   473	Splitting itself does not invalidate an algebra identity: one specializes in
   474	the product algebra and checks the recorded resultants. What is invalid is to
   475	call every specialized quotient a field or silently invert a zero divisor.
   476	This is the required FALLACY-v2 distinction between a generic identity and
   477	its specializations.
   478	
   479	## 6. Controls and theorem status
   480	
   481	Every accepted full-chart exact run extracts the ideal component returned by
   482	`sat()`, asserts its type and declared ring, and passes both controls
   483	
   484	```text
   485	EMPTY:    <c>:<c>^infinity = <1>,
   486	NONEMPTY: <c-1>:<c>^infinity != <1>,
   487	```
   488	
   489	or their equivalent Rabinowitsch presentations. Every normalized ring first
   490	proves the displayed image of `c` is a unit and repeats positive and negative
   491	wrapper controls in that declared coefficient ring. Completed stderr streams
   492	are empty.
   493	
   494	The semantic negative classifier is
   495	
   496	```text
   497	(F,G)=(pi,pi-gamma^2/2), J(F,G)=gamma.
   498	```
   499	
   500	It passes both reciprocal quadratic-anchor shapes, but its pi-degrees are
   501	`(1,1)` and it has none of the K=16 degree/tuple data. Hence it fails the
   502	tuple and is never inserted as a target-chart point.
   503	
   504	Monic h-division keeps zero remainders and never divides by a
   505	parameter-dependent leader. Prime marks remain labels unless the source
   506	defines differentiation. No cv flag, place, or series is identified; no
   507	carrier or attainment assertion is made. No exit set or exit price is
   508	asserted, so no `charge_basis=...` line is due.
   509	
   510	The fixed rows now have the following status:
   511	
   512	- `t=1`: **PROVED-HERE**, exact normalized unit and full-chart `[1]`.
   513	- `t=2`: **PROVED-HERE**, both exact split fibers and full-chart `[1]`.
   514	- `t=3`: **PROVED-HERE**, exact six-generator quadratic-field `[1]` replay.
   515	- `t=4`: `PENDING_T4_STATUS`.
   516	- all `t>=1`: **PARTIAL / OPEN[T-UNIFORM-MIDDLE]**.
   517	
   518	The bounded next step is to prove the second affine recurrence by induction on
   519	the band index, recording every pivot norm, then derive the growing
   520	`2t`-row/`t`-variable terminal family and seek a terminal recurrence ending in
   521	a nonzero coefficient-algebra constant. Finite additional samples cannot
   522	replace that induction.
   523	
   524	## 7. Principal reproduction
   525	
