   312	## 3. Exact fixed-`t` structures
   313	
   314	The “Q pivots” below are the charged characteristic-zero constant-pivot spine;
   315	the “A pivots” are affine eliminations whose coefficients have explicit
   316	inverses in the stated rank-two algebra. Every substitution was reduced and
   317	checked modulo `H_t`. Degrees are total degrees in the final chart unknowns,
   318	with `y` in the coefficient algebra.
   319	
   320	| `t` | full rows / unknowns | Q pivots; quotient rows / unknowns | primitive `H_t`; disc | post-H/c rows / auxiliaries | A pivots | terminal system |
   321	|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|---|
   322	| 1 | 23 / 18 | 7; 15 / 11 | `54y^2-36y+5`; 216 | 11 / 8 | 4 then unit | `[1]` |
   323	| 2 | 37 / 27 | 10; 26 / 17 | `25y^2-15y+2`; 25 | 20 / 14 | 12 | 4 rows / 2 vars |
   324	| 3 | 51 / 36 | 13; 37 / 23 | `147y^2-84y+11`; 588 | 29 / 20 | 17 | 6 rows / 3 vars |
   325	| 4 | 65 / 45 | 16; 48 / 29 | `486y^2-270y+35`; 4860 | 38 / 26 | 22 | 8 rows / 4 vars |
   326	
   327	### 3.1 `t=1`: `(16,12;13;3)`
   328	
   329	Here `x=q2_1`, `y=q3_1`, and
   330	
   331	```text
   332	H_1=54y^2-36y+5,
   333	c=-4y(9y-1)/81.
   334	```
   335	
   336	After four checked affine pivots the normalized system contains the
   337	coefficient-field constant
   338	
   339	```text
   340	20y-10/3, inverse 27/10-27y/5 modulo H_1.
   341	```
   342	
   343	Thus its ideal is `[1]` before any multivariate basis computation. The
   344	normalized and full gauged exact Singular replays both return `[1]` with all
   345	controls passing. This is consistent with Moh's `(16,12)` conclusion but does
   346	not attribute this unprinted elimination to Moh. It also explains why `t=1`
   347	does not have the later terminal pattern: the boundary regimes of the
   348	coefficient table collide and an early unit appears.
   349	
   350	### 3.2 `t=2`: `(28,20;25;3)`
   351	
   352	Here `x=q3_1`, `y=q5_1`, and
   353	
   354	```text
   355	H_2=(5y-1)(5y-2),
   356	c=-7y(10y-1)/125.
   357	```
   358	
   359	The two fibers are
   360	
   361	```text
   362	y=1/5, c=-7/625;     y=2/5, c=-42/625.
   363	```
   364	
   365	Neither is discarded. Twelve common-algebra unit pivots and four zero-row
   366	reductions leave four generators in `(b3,b4)`, one at each band
   367	`h=0,1,2,3`, of degrees `9,8,7,6`. Independent rational-fiber presentations
   368	are printed in `box/k16uniform-20260903/t2_t1_audit.md`; exact Singular `std`
   369	returns `[1]` on each. The full 37-row gauged saturation independently
   370	returns `[1]`.
   371	
   372	This alone refutes the proposed literal residual: the safe gauge is
   373	`alpha_t=alpha_2=0`, so `a2_0` is not even a `t=2` chart variable.
   374	
   375	### 3.3 `t=3`: `(40,28;37;3)`
   376	
   377	Here `x=q4_1`, `y=q7_1`, and
   378	
   379	```text
   380	H_3=147y^2-84y+11,
   381	c=10y(2-21y)/343.
   382	```
   383	
   384	The fresh replay starts from the frozen charged drivers, repeats the thirteen
   385	Q pivots, removes six exact Q-associate duplicates and the `H_3` row, and
   386	uses seventeen checked A-pivots. It leaves exactly six generators in
   387	`(b3,b4,a2_0)`, one at each band `h=0,...,5`, with degrees
   388	`13,12,11,10,9,8`. Their complete coefficients are in
   389	`box/k16uniform-20260903/t3_residual_generators.tsv` (SHA-256
   390	`c09d9f0b8b7e763734c42d5c7cf69ca9adfd41d25ae53a3dbbbe1896badacae1`).
   391	
   392	The exact replay input has SHA-256
   393	`fc2c504604c51e33e7c63e32bde4a952d0c6741b99fcf5e9c334c63eefb4796b`,
   394	identical to the charged decisive input. Singular 4.3.2 `std` returns
   395	
   396	```text
   397	MAIN_START ... residual_equations=6 residual_unknowns=3
   398	MAIN_DONE basis_size=
   399	1
   400	MAIN_QUADRATIC_FIELD_EMPTY
   401	G[1]=1
   402	```
   403	
   404	in 0.06 s with 12,988 KiB maximum RSS and empty stderr.
   405	
   406	### 3.4 `t=4`: `(52,36;49;3)`
   407	
   408	Here `x=q5_1`, `y=q9_1`, and
   409	
   410	```text
   411	H_4=486y^2-270y+35,
   412	c=y(130-1404y)/2187.
   413	```
   414	
   415	Sixteen exact Q-pivots reduce the 65-row/45-unknown chart to 48 rows in 29
   416	unknowns. After the slice, exact duplicate removal, and passage to
   417	`Q[y]/(H_4)`, there are 38 rows in 26 auxiliaries. Twenty-two further
   418	unit-only affine pivots leave eight generators in four variables
   419	`(b3,b4,a2_0,q3_0)`, one at each band `h=0,...,7`, all with remainder tag
   420	`(gamma_power,pi_power)=(0,1)`, and degrees `17,16,...,10`. The appearance of
   421	`q3_0` rather than `a3_0` is a valid pivot-coordinate choice, not an invariant
   422	naming claim.
   423	
   424	This residual closes exactly in characteristic zero. Since
   425	
   426	```text
   427	486*((15+sqrt15)/54)^2-270*((15+sqrt15)/54)+35
   428	  =(sqrt15^2-15)/6,
   429	```
   430	
   431	the maps `y -> (15+sqrt15)/54` and `sqrt15 -> 54y-15` identify
   432	`Q[y]/(H_4)` with `Q(sqrt15)`. Thus this is an isomorphism of the abstract
   433	coefficient fields, not a choice that loses the conjugate root. The complete
   434	eight-generator input
   435	`box/k16uniform-20260903/t4_exact_Qsqrt15_nfmodstd.sing` has SHA-256
   436	`6b2f8f0eafe2792b99ede7d902504a34a9a8ce7096df7d948b441e97936421cf`.
   437	Singular's exact number-field `nfmodStd` returns
   438	
   439	```text
   440	MAIN_START t=4 field=Qsqrt15 rows=8 vars=4 method=nfmodStd
   441	MAIN_DONE basis_size=
   442	1
   443	MAIN_EXACT_UNIT
   444	G[1]=1
   445	```
   446	
   447	in 0.82 s with 15,532 KiB maximum RSS and empty stderr. Its actual-pair,
   448	`c`-unit, ring/type, and EMPTY/NONEMPTY controls pass separately in the
   449	rational ambient ring, the coefficient ring, and the final residual ring.
   450	Because every preceding pivot is a checked coefficient-field unit and the
   451	weighted slice is equivalent on `c!=0`, this proves the exact t=4 chart empty.
   452	
   453	The previously charged full-chart bases `[1]` over three good primes remain
   454	**MEASURED-MODULAR** cross-checks only; they are not used to promote the
   455	characteristic-zero conclusion.
   456	
   457	## 4. The residual pattern and the exact blocker
   458	
   459	### 4.1 What the finite systems actually say
   460	
   461	The proposed statement
   462	
   463	```text
   464	six generators in (b3,b4,a2_0), bands 0,...,5, for every t
   465	```
   466	
   467	is false, not merely unproved. Both `t=1` and `t=2` are counterexamples to
   468	that presentation; at `t=2`, `a2_0` is eliminated by the required gauge.
   469	
   470	The exact `t=2,3,4` reductions instead exhibit the tentative linear pattern
   471	
   472	```text
   473	post-H/c input:       9t+2 rows in 6t+2 auxiliaries,
   474	affine pivots:        5t+2,
   475	zero/duplicate rows:  2t,
   476	terminal:             2t rows in t variables,
   477	bands:                0,...,2t-1,
   478	degrees:              4t+1,...,2t+2.
   479	```
   480	
   481	This is exact for the three displayed integers, but is **not** promoted as an
   482	all-`t` theorem. Residual coordinate names depend on the chosen valid pivot
   483	sequence, and no closed second-spine recurrence has been proved.
   484	
   485	### 4.2 Smallest proved uniform statement
   486	
   487	The following much smaller statement is proved uniformly:
   488	
   489	1. The banded chart, coefficient spaces, and three gauges are valid for all
   490	   `t>=1` and contain no parameter denominators.
   491	2. There are `3t+4` Q-constant quotient pivots, descending from band
   492	   `4t+1` through band `2t`. The gauged chart has `9t+9` variables, so this
   493	   leaves `6t+5` before the weighted slice.
   494	3. The positive grading, equations (H) and (C), the `x=1` equivalence, and
   495	   the c-unit statement in the separable algebra `A_t` hold for every
   496	   positive integer `t`.
   497	4. No fixed collection of low bands, or of low plus a fixed number of
   498	   extreme-high bands, can supply a uniform unit certificate: the charged
   499	   exact point
   500	   `Q=h^q+B, P=h^e+2pi-gamma, c=-1` satisfies all low levels through
   501	   `2t-1` and fails only at the moving bands `2t` and `3t+1`.
   502	
   503	The missing object is the **second affine spine in the t-scaling middle**.
   504	After passage to `A_t`, every proposed pivot coefficient is an element
   505	`u_(t,j)(y)`. A uniform quotient-ring elimination must give a closed formula
   506	or recurrence for these elements and prove
   507	
   508	```text
   509	Norm_(A_t/Q)(u_(t,j)) != 0
   510	    iff Res_y(H_t,u_(t,j)) != 0.
   511	```
   512	
   513	(For the displayed nonmonic `H_t`, norm and resultant can differ by a
   514	nonzero rational power of its leading coefficient.)
   515	
   516	for every required band index and every positive integer `t`. It must also
   517	prove the observed duplicate/zero recurrence and identify the t-dependent
   518	terminal ideal. The coefficient-space boundaries move at low band `t` and at
   519	high offset `t`; this is precisely where the charts for `t` and `t+1` first
   520	differ. Thus the normalizer is no longer the blocker. The t-dependent middle
   521	system is.
   522	
   523	## 5. Why a generic-`t` `[1]` is not presently available
   524	
   525	There is no fixed six-by-three residual `R_t` to enter in
   526	`Q(t)[y]/(H_t)`: the verified `t=2,3,4` terminal rings already refute that
   527	fixed presentation and have observed growing sizes. One could encode the
   528	systems by an indexed recurrence, but that recurrence is the open
   529	second-spine problem just named. Consequently no generic Gröbner basis was
   530	computed and no finite exceptional denominator set is asserted.
   531	
   532	If a future recurrence or genuinely fixed reformulation does yield
   533	
   534	```text
   535	1=sum_i A_i(t,y,u) R_i(t,y,u)+B(t,y,u)H_t(y)
   536	```
   537	
   538	in `Q(t)[y,u_1,...,u_r]`, FALLACY-v2 requires clearing a common nonzero denominator
   539	`D(t)`. The certificate specializes only when `D(t0)` and the leading
   540	coefficient of `H_t0` are nonzero. Every inverted `A_t` coefficient must
   541	contribute its norm/resultant to `D`, and every integer root of `D` must be
   542	handled exactly.
   543	
   544	The infinite split set `t=3s^2-1` is not a finite denominator-exception set.
   545	Splitting itself does not invalidate an algebra identity: one specializes in
   546	the product algebra and checks the recorded resultants. What is invalid is to
   547	call every specialized quotient a field or silently invert a zero divisor.
   548	This is the required FALLACY-v2 distinction between a generic identity and
   549	its specializations.
   550	
   551	## 6. Controls and theorem status
   552	
   553	Every accepted full-chart exact run extracts the ideal component returned by
   554	`sat()`, asserts its type and declared ring, and passes both controls
   555	
   556	```text
   557	EMPTY:    <c>:<c>^infinity = <1>,
   558	NONEMPTY: <c-1>:<c>^infinity != <1>,
   559	```
   560	
   561	or their equivalent Rabinowitsch presentations. Every normalized ring first
   562	proves the displayed image of `c` is a unit and repeats positive and negative
   563	wrapper controls in that declared coefficient ring. No completed output has a
   564	CAS error marker; files used to capture `/usr/bin/time` contain resource data,
   565	not a silent algebra failure.
   566	
   567	The semantic negative classifier is
   568	
   569	```text
   570	(F,G)=(pi,pi-gamma^2/2), J(F,G)=gamma.
   571	```
   572	
   573	It passes both reciprocal quadratic-anchor shapes, but its pi-degrees are
   574	`(1,1)` and it has none of the K=16 degree/tuple data. Hence it fails the
   575	tuple and is never inserted as a target-chart point.
   576	
   577	Monic h-division keeps zero remainders and never divides by a
   578	parameter-dependent leader. Prime marks remain labels unless the source
   579	defines differentiation. No cv flag, place, or series is identified; no
   580	carrier or attainment assertion is made. No exit set or exit price is
   581	asserted, so no `charge_basis=...` line is due.
   582	
   583	The fixed rows now have the following status:
   584	
   585	- `t=1`: **PROVED-HERE**, exact normalized unit and full-chart `[1]`.
   586	- `t=2`: **PROVED-HERE**, both exact split fibers and full-chart `[1]`.
   587	- `t=3`: **PROVED-HERE**, exact six-generator quadratic-field `[1]` replay.
   588	- `t=4`: **PROVED-HERE**, exact eight-generator `Q(sqrt15)` basis `[1]`.
   589	- all `t>=1`: **PARTIAL / OPEN[T-UNIFORM-MIDDLE]**.
   590	
   591	The bounded next step is to prove the second affine recurrence by induction on
   592	the band index, recording every pivot norm, then prove or refute the observed
   593	`2t`-row/`t`-variable terminal family and seek a terminal recurrence ending in
   594	a nonzero coefficient-algebra constant. Finite additional samples cannot
   595	replace that induction.
   596	
   597	## 7. Principal reproduction
   598	
